<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Naviglio Grande</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1177">1177</a>–<a href="/years/1272">1272</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Naviglio Grande is a canal in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a>, about 50 km long, that carries water from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ticino">Ticino</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>. Begun in the late twelfth century as an irrigation channel and made navigable in the thirteenth, it irrigated the surrounding plain and brought marble for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan-cathedral">Milan Cathedral</a> to the city. It is the oldest of the Navigli, the canal network that linked Milan with Lake Maggiore, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-como">Lake Como</a> and the Po.</p></div>
